  "policy": [
    "This list is fixed before scoring and is NOT extended after hearing engine output.",
    "A term is counted only where the reference transcript contains it, so adding a term the corpus does not contain changes nothing, and removing one after seeing results would be metric tuning.",
    "`accept` holds every spelling that counts as a correct recognition, in the normalisation of harness.normalize.normalize_term (case-folded, punctuation dropped, hyphens split, Russian inflectional tails stripped from Latin stems).",
    "A Cyrillic transliteration is deliberately NOT accepted for a Latin-script term: `Кликхаус` for ClickHouse is the exact failure mode the employer reported, and counting it as a hit would define the problem away. It is scored as a Latin-to-Cyrillic substitution.",
    "Terms are matched as token n-grams, so a multi-word term such as `feature store` is one term occurrence, not two.",
    "Where Russian declension replaces a Latin stem's final vowel (Kafka -> Kafkу), the shortened stem is listed explicitly as an accepted form. It is never derived by a general rule: a rule that drops any final Latin vowel would fold Kafko onto Kafka and score a mangled product name as a correct one."
  ],
